{"type":"after","callId":"call@102","endTime":46679.482,"result":{"value":{"s":"\n    Home/Manual/Fix, mod & accessorise/FAQ\n    \n\nFAQ\nThe questions owners ask first.\n✅bench📖official👥communityLast verified 2026-08-27View as Markdown\nWhat the badges mean✅bench Verified on our bench📖official Official Battle Company docs🔍app Decoded from the Callsign app👥community Community-reported🧪software Built + software-tested📐spec Specified only🚧under construction Under constructionNothing unconfirmed is published — see Credits & sourcing.\n\nWhy won't my gun fire?Check the headset first: it's off, unpaired (slow rainbow blink) or dropped mid-game, and the firmware locks the trigger. Link it, or re-pair. Second most common: the game hasn't started (pull the reload handle) or you're dead. ✅bench📖official👥community\nHow do I re-pair a headset?Headset on, hold its small button, boot the tagger holding RIGHT, wait for \"PAIRING MODE\", pull the trigger once (\"HEADSET CONNECTED\") and once more (\"device paired\"). 👥community\nThe headset went dark once the game started — is it broken?No. Team colour shows pre-game only; dark during play is native. Rainbow is the fault state. ✅bench\nCan I put custom sounds on the tagger?Yes. Hold SELECT while powering on with the programming port plugged into a computer; a drive appears with an  folder — replace the  files (slow: ~1 h per 250 MB). Keep the originals. 📖official👥community\nWhich phones work with the official app?Callsign works on Android 10 and older, not on newer Android. On any phone the headset must be linked or the app disconnects. 👥community✅bench\nWhat battery and charger does it take?A 7.4 V ~2200 mAh Li-ion pack with an 8.4 V two-cell smart charger; the headset charges from any 5 V USB. Optional 6×AA — non-rechargeable only. 📖official👥community\nIs the battery polarity really reversed?Yes — reversed from the usual convention. Meter any replacement pack before plugging it in. 👥community\nWhy is my gun called Tactix2 again?Opening the official app resets the owner-set name. Rename it and power-cycle. ✅bench\nWhy do guns fail after about an hour of hosted play?\"Screamers\": a documented failure of taggers left powered and hosted for long sessions, plus a firmware rule that refuses Bluetooth re-pairing below a battery threshold. Power-rest guns, rotate them, keep batteries topped. 👥community✅bench\nDo I have to open the gun for JEDGE?No. It rides on the phone bracket with its own power; stock firmware is never touched. The Open BRX Companion is designed the same way. 👥community\nCan I change the grenade's mode from an app?No — it's set only by the button-hold on the device, and it stays set across power cycles. 👥community✅bench\nWhere do I get 3D-print files?There is no public BRX library yet; the reload-button STL circulates in the owners' group. Open BRX is building an open, versioned one. 👥community\nSource: pages above\n\n\n  "}},"afterSnapshot":"after@call@102"}
